<title>RUSSIA: Rostelekom raises pref dividend, omits ordinary.</title>
<headline>Rostelekom raises pref dividend, omits ordinary.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian long-distance telecoms company Rostelekom is raising its dividend on preferred shares to 475.61 roubles, or 19,024.40 percent of the 2.50 nominal value, for 1996 from 446.75 roubles or 17,870 percent for 1995, a senior company official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Igor Kocheshkov, head of investor relations, told Reuters that AOOT Mezhdugorodnoi i Mezhdunarodnoi Elektricheskoi Svyazi Rostelekom would again forego a dividend on ordinary shares.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
